SUMMARY:Lec73|Quantum Computing with Oscillators and Qubits|Yuan Liu-North Carolina State University
LOCATION:https://tinyurl.com/gucs-zoom
DESCRIPTION:Hardware platforms based on native continuous-variable (CV\, oscillator) systems have attracted growing attention as an alternative to discrete-variable (DV\, qubit) quantum systems. In this talk\, I will highlight how hybrid CV-DV hardware offers a powerful computational paradigm by combining the complementary strengths of both CV and DV processors. I will present novel quantum control techniques and algorithms for CV-DV systems that enable new opportunities and applications in quantum error correction\, quantum simulation\, and quantum sensing. I will also highlight software tools for benchmarking and compiling these novel processors.
URL:https://qucs.info/lectures/73-quantum-computing-with-oscillators-and-qubits
